cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "Finite Forward-Iterate Schröder Approximation from Geometric Richardson Extrapolation: Reciprocal Filters and Exact Paired Remainders"

type: article

authors:
  - family-names: "Baker"
    given-names: "Wayne"

version: "0.2.1"

date-released: 2026-10-03

abstract: >-
  This work develops a finite forward-iterate realization of geometric
  Richardson extrapolation through Schröder conjugacy. It establishes
  reciprocal composition-side and scale-side filters, exact paired
  remainder identities, explicit first-surviving coefficients,
  active-mode uniqueness criteria, finite exact recovery, and a
  sine/arcsine specialization associated with classical Chebyshev
  multiple-angle polynomials.

license: "CC-BY-4.0"

repository-code: "https://github.com/CWBaker360/finite-forward-iterate-schroeder-richardson"

keywords:
  - Schröder equation
  - Richardson extrapolation
  - Koenigs linearization
  - functional iteration
  - composition operators
  - reciprocal filters
  - approximation theory
  - Chebyshev polynomials
